 "title": "Corporate partnerships for environmental impact| FNPW",
 "status": 200,
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "figcaption",
   "v": "Photo by Carol Carter & Allan Chawner"
  },
  {
   "t": "h1",
   "v": "Corporate Partnerships for Environmental Impact"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "We work with corporate, government and not-for-profit partners to protect natural Australia for future generations."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "As leaders in Corporate Social Responsibility, our partners engage with FNPW to make a meaningful impact for the Australian environment. The aim is to preserve natural resources and protect endangered habitats and species."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "Partnering with FNPW allows you to take a leadership role in promoting environmental sustainability and environmentally responsible practices while helping FNPW reach conservation goals for Australian wildlife."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "We would love to speak with you to learn more about your company, your goals, and to explore possible partnership opportunities with FNPW."
  },
  {
   "t": "h2",
   "v": "Major partners"
  },
  {
   "t": "h2",
   "v": "Supporting Partners"
  },
  {
   "t": "h2",
   "v": "Testimonials"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "“One Tree Planted is proud to be the headline partner for the Foundation for National Parks & Wildlife major project to plant one million trees in bushfire affected areas across Australia by 2025. This valuable partnership strengthens our mission to get more trees planted around the world and raise awareness of the importance of healthy forests. This project is key to regeneration in areas that were badly affected by the Black Summer bushfires and we are working closely with FNPW to ensure success of this important project.”"
  },
  {
   "t": "h3",
   "v": "Beth Dalgleish"
  },
  {
   "t": "h4",
   "v": "One Tree Planted"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "“L’Occitane is proud to partner with the Foundation for National Parks & Wildlife to plant one million trees in bushfire affected areas across Australia by 2025. Together, we are working with local communities to plant thousands of native seedlings in existing nurseries to be placed in bushfire affected areas and restore wildlife habitats for future generations. As a brand originated from nature and the use of botanical ingredients, it has long been a commitment of ours to respect and support biodiversity, and we see this project as a vital step towards our goal to protect 1,000 threatened species and varieties of plants globally.”"
  },
  {
   "t": "h3",
   "v": "Pierre-Emmanuel Joffre"
  },
  {
   "t": "h4",
   "v": "L’OCCITANE Australia"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "“As part of our bushfire response, Sonic Healthcare partnered with the Foundation for National Parks & Wildlife (FNPW) to give an immediate funding boost to wildlife care and bushland regeneration programs. Sonic is proud to have partnered with FNPW to facilitate this vital recovery work.”"
  },
  {
   "t": "h3",
   "v": "Diane Harari"
  },
  {
   "t": "h4",
   "v": "Sonic Healthcare"
  },
  {
   "t": "h2",
   "v": "How we work with partners"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "We work with corporate, government and not-for-profit partners to protect natural Australia for future generations."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "Our partners fund important projects like Bushfire Recovery Nurseries, Wildlife Heroes, and more…"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "We also offer Corporate Volunteering opportunities"
  },
  {
   "t": "h3",
   "v": "Talk to us to discuss a partnership"
  },
  {
